From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elaina <elaina@k230>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: toggle Yahboom backlight without resetting panel

The universal panel driver owns the LCD_EN GPIO. Keep it synchronized with
DRM panel enable/disable so X11 DPMS can turn the physical backlight off.
Keep the reset line high during DPMS transitions so boot-console handoff and
display resume do not leave the panel uninitialized.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-canaan-universal.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-canaan-universal.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-canaan-universal.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-canaan-universal.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-canaan-universal.c
@@ -152,8 +152,18 @@ static int canaan_panel_enable(struct drm_panel *panel)
 {
+	struct canaan_panel *p = panel_to_canaan_panel(panel);
+
+	if (p->power_on)
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(p->power_on, 1);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
 static int canaan_panel_disable(struct drm_panel *panel)
 {
+	struct canaan_panel *p = panel_to_canaan_panel(panel);
+
+	if (p->power_on)
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(p->power_on, 0);
+
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -169,9 +177,7 @@ static int canaan_panel_unprepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 	if (p->power_on)
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(p->power_on, 0);
-	if (p->reset)
-		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(p->reset, 0);
 
 	panel_simple_sleep(500);
 
 	return 0;
 }
